        "descriptionModule": {
          "briefSummary": "The goal of this YH42946-101 is to evaluate the safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics and anti-tumor activity of YH42946 in patients with locally advanced of metastatic solid tumors with HER2 aberration and EGFR exon 20 insertions.",
          "detailedDescription": "YH42946 is a novel, orally available tyrosine kinase inhibitor targeting HER2. YH42946 showed potency for diverse HER2 aberrations including HER2 overexpression, amplification, or mutation, as well as EGFR Ex20ins.\n\nThis is a Phase 1/2, open-label, multicenter, first-in-human study of YH42946. The study has 2 parts. The first part is dose escalation part to identify the maximum tolerated dose. The second part is dose expansion part to select 2 doses for RD selection at the first cohort, after then RD will be determined to ensure its efficacy. Several independent cohorts are planned."
        },
