        "descriptionModule": {
          "briefSummary": "The objective of this study is to evaluate the safety, tolerability, and efficacy of BL-B01D1 in patients with Metastatic or Unresectable Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC) and Other Solid Tumors.",
          "detailedDescription": "BL-B01D1-LUNG-101 is a global, multi-center, Phase 1 study to evaluate the safety, tolerability, pharmacokinetics , and initial efficacy of BL-B01D1 in participants with metastatic or unresectable NSCLC and Other Solid Tumors.\n\nThis study will be conducted in two different dosing schedules (Cohort A and Cohort B) and three parts (dose escalation, dose finding and dose expansion). Cohort A will be dosed on Day 1 and Day 8 of a continuous 21-day treatment cycle. Cohort B will be dosed on Day 1 of a continuous 21-day treatment cycle. Each Cohort has different dose groups."
        },
