                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "analyses": [
                {
                  "groupIds": [
                    "OG000",
                    "OG001"
                  ],
                  "groupDescription": "The statistical hypotheses, null hypothesis (H0) and alternate hypothesis (H1), are stated below:\n\nH0: μLEV = μPBO vs. H1: μLEV ≠ μPBO\n\nANCOVA on the endpoint \"percentage change from Combined Baseline of GTC seizures per week\" using \"treatment\" and \"country\" as factors (categorical predictors) and \"Combined Baseline GTC seizure frequency per week\" as a covariate (a continuous predictor) where μLEV and μPBO are adjusted means for LEV and PBO, respectively.",
                  "nonInferiorityType": "SUPERIORITY_OR_OTHER_LEGACY",
                  "pValue": "<0.0001",
                  "pValueComment": "Statistical testing was 2-sided, and was performed using a significance (α) level of 0.05.",
                  "statisticalMethod": "ANCOVA",
                  "paramType": "Mean Difference (Net)",
                  "paramValue": "-56.13",
                  "ciPctValue": "95",
                  "ciNumSides": "TWO_SIDED",
                  "ciLowerLimit": "-68.24",
                  "ciUpperLimit": "-44.02",
                  "dispersionType": "STANDARD_ERROR_OF_MEAN",
                  "dispersionValue": "6.15"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "SECONDARY",
              "title": "The Percentage Change in Generalized Tonic-clonic Seizure Frequency Per Week From the Combined Baseline Over the Evaluation Period",
              "description": "Percentage change in generalized tonic-clonic (GTC) seizure frequency per week from combined baseline B over the Evaluation Period A is calculated using the equation:\n\nPercentage change from Baseline = ((A-B)/B)\\*100. Percentage change from baseline is not defined for subjects whose baseline Information is missing / unknown or equal to zero, or whose seizure frequency per week is missing / unknown. A negative value in change in generalized tonic-clonic (GTC) seizure frequency indicates a reduction of generalized tonic-clonic (GTC) seizure frequency.\n\nCombined Baseline means: a 4-week Retrospective Baseline + 4-week Prospective Baseline or 8-week Prospective Baseline.",
              "populationDescription": "Of the 226 subjects in the Full Analysis Set (FAS), 205 are included in the analysis of this Outcome Measure in Evaluation Period.",
              "reportingStatus": "POSTED",
              "paramType": "MEAN",
              "dispersionType": "Standard Deviation",
              "unitOfMeasure": "Percentage Change",
