        "armsInterventionsModule": {
          "armGroups": [
            {
              "label": "Lacosamide",
              "type": "EXPERIMENTAL",
              "description": "Lacosamide will be added to levetiracetam while withdrawing the sodium channel blocking antiepileptic drug (AED)",
              "interventionNames": [
                "Drug: Lacosamide"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "interventions": [
            {
              "type": "DRUG",
              "name": "Lacosamide",
              "description": "50 mg and 100 mg lacosamide tablets will be combined and taken in two equal doses per day to provide the required total daily dosage of 100 - 600 mg/day. Subjects were titrated to a minimum of 200 mg/ day during the Treatment Period.\n\nMaximum duration of study drug administration is approximately 23 weeks.",
              "armGroupLabels": [
                "Lacosamide"
              ],
              "otherNames": [
                "VIMPAT®",
                "SPM927",
                "Harkoseride"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "outcomesModule": {
          "primaryOutcomes": [
            {
              "measure": "Retention at the End of the 21-week Treatment Period",
              "description": "Retention is a summary measure that integrates both the patient's and clinician's assessment of efficacy and tolerability in epilepsy clinical studies to provide a measure of effectiveness.",
              "timeFrame": "Duration of the Treatment Period (21 Weeks)"
            }
          ]
        },
        "eligibilityModule": {
          "eligibilityCriteria": "Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Subject is male or female, at least 18 years of age\n* Subject has a diagnosis of epilepsy with partial-onset seizures according to the International Classification of Epileptic Seizures (1981)\n* Subject is taking levetiracetam (LEV) in combination with 1 sodium channel blocking antiepileptic drug (defined as carbamazepine, lamotrigine, oxcarbazepine, phenytoin, or eslicarbazepine) as adjunctive treatment for epilepsy\n* The minimum required seizure frequency during the 8-week Retrospective Seizure Baseline is on average ≥ 2 partial-onset seizures per 28 days with at least 1 seizure per 4 week period within the 8-week Retrospective Seizure Baseline. Additionally, subjects must experience at least 1 seizure during the 4-week Prospective Seizure Baseline\n* Subject has been maintained on a stable dose of LEV and a sodium channel blocking antiepileptic drug (SCB-AED) for at least 4 weeks prior to the Screening Visit (Visit 1) and during the 4-week Prospective Seizure Baseline\n* The minimum required seizure frequency during the 8-week Retrospective Seizure Baseline is on average ≥ 2 partial-onset seizures per 28 days (based on investigator assessment of subject report) with at least 1 seizure per 4 week period within the 8-week Retrospective Seizure Baseline\n* Subject has been maintained on a stable dose of levetiracetam (LEV) and a sodium channel blocking antiepileptic drug (SCB-AED) for at least 4 weeks prior to the Screening Visit (Visit 1) and during the 4-week Prospective Seizure Baseline, with or without additional concurrent stable vagal nerve stimulation (VNS). The VNS must have been in place for at least 6 months prior to the Screening Visit (Visit 1) with constant settings for at least 4-weeks prior to the Screening Visit (Visit 1) and throughout the duration of the study\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Previous use of lacosamide\n* History of alcohol or drug abuse\n* History of seizure disorder characterized primarily by isolated auras\n* History of primary generalized seizures\n* History of status epilepticus within the 12-months\n* History of clustering seizures\n* Nonepileptic events, including pseudoseizures that could be confused with seizures\n* History of any medical or psychiatric condition that, in the opinion of the investigator, could jeopardize the subject's health or would compromise the subject's ability to participate in this study\n* Lifetime history of suicide attempt, or suicidal ideation in the past 6 months\n* Hypersensitivity to any component of lacosamide (LCM)\n* History of acute or sub-acute progressive central nervous system disease\n* History of severe anaphylactic reaction or serious blood dyscrasias\n* Impaired renal function (ie, Creatinine Clearance (CLcr) is lower than 30 mL/min) at Visit 1\n* History of sick sinus syndrome without a pacemaker, or atrioventricular (AV) block, or subject has any other clinically significant electrocardiogram (ECG) abnormalities\n* History sodium channelopathy, such as Brugada syndrome\n* History of myocardial infarction in the last 3 months",
          "healthyVolunteers": false,
          "sex": "ALL",
          "minimumAge": "18 Years",
          "stdAges": [
            "ADULT",
            "OLDER_ADULT"
          ]
